[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:It's Only Me]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.63]Lesson 13 | 第13课
[00:02.84]'It's only me' | “是我呀”
[00:10.87]What did the man expect to find under the stairs? | 那个人以为楼梯下藏着什么？
[00:16.42]After her husband had gone to work, Mrs. Richards sent her children to school and went upstairs to her bedroom. | 理查兹夫人送走了上班的丈夫，打发孩子们上了学，便回到楼上自己的卧室里。
[00:24.96]She was too excited to do any housework that morning, for in the evening she would be going to a fancy-dress party with her husband. | 那天早上她兴奋得无心做家务，因为晚上她要和丈夫一起去参加一个化装舞会。
[00:34.89]She intended to dress up as a ghost and as she had made her costume the night before, she was impatient to try it on. | 她打算装扮成鬼，由于头天晚上已把戏服做好，她迫不及待地想试穿一下。
[00:44.23]Though the costume consisted only of a sheet, it was very effective. | 尽管那身戏服只是一条床单，效果却很不错。
[00:49.62]After putting it on, Mrs. Richards went downstairs. | 穿好后，理查兹夫人下了楼。
[00:53.93]She wanted to find out whether it would be comfortable to wear. | 她想看看穿着它舒服不舒服。
[00:58.27]Just as Mrs. Richards was entering the dining-room, there was a knock on the front door. | 理查兹夫人刚要进餐厅，前门响起了敲门声。
[01:04.84]She knew that it must be the baker. | 她知道一定是面包师来了。
[01:07.48]She had told him to come straight in if ever she failed to open the door and to leave the bread on the kitchen table. | 她曾告诉过面包师，如果她没来开门，就径直进屋，把面包放在厨房的桌子上。
[01:14.42]Not wanting to frighten the poor man, Mrs. Richards quickly hid in the small storeroom under the stairs. | 理查兹夫人不想吓着可怜的面包师，便赶紧躲到了楼梯下的小储藏室里。
[01:22.13]She heard the front door open and heavy footsteps in the hall. | 她听见前门开了，大厅里响起沉重的脚步声。
[01:27.05]Suddenly the door of the storeroom was opened and a man entered. | 突然，储藏室的门被打开，一个男子走了进来。
[01:31.48]Mrs. Richards realized that it must be the man from the Electricity Board who had come to read the metre. | 理查兹夫人意识到这一定是来查电表的电力公司的人。
[01:38.78]She tried to explain the situation, saying | 她想解释一下情况，说：
[01:42.15]'It's only me', but it was too late. | “是我呀”，可是已经来不及了。
[01:46.49]The man let out a cry and jumped back several paces. | 那男子大叫一声，向后倒退了好几步。
[01:51.82]When Mrs. Richards walked towards him, he fled, slamming the door behind him. | 理查兹夫人朝他走去时，他夺路而逃，随手“砰”地把门关上了。
